join detective (Speaking) right
detective: Hello.
join cook left
cook: Hey.
detective: I'm here to ask you some questions about the murder.
cook: I figured.
- Who are you?
	detective: Mind introducing yourself?
	cook: Name’s [COOK]. I make food for Dracula. Or, did, rather.
	detective: Food, huh? Wasn’t he having a dinner party before he died?
	cook: Whatever you’re implying, you’re at the wrong address. 
	detective: Mighty defensive.
	cook: Listen, I don’t get why we need some big investigation for all this. Drac’s dead, and some other blood-sucker is taking his place for the next 400 years until the same thing happens to them. 
	detective: You don't like Dracula very much, do you?
	cook: It’s nothing personal. Vampires in general get under my skin.
	cook: In the metaphorical sense, that is.
	detective: Yet you work for one?
	cook: Someone has to pay my bills, and I don’t know if you noticed, but Drac's pretty loaded— er, was.
